--- a/freecad_s1/ext/mixed.py
+++ b/freecad_s1/ext/mixed.py
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@ normal nz=+1 and z (sometimes also "at"). Before this patch nz=+1 only ever came
 so a model read any nz=+1 as a datum plane (the S 80 casing built its top flange on
 Plane:XY instead of Face+Z).
 
+Patch 0017 (training goals only; the suites keep their goals): a stack's flange may carry up to
+three bolt holes, each mirrored (hole, mirror, hole, mirror), as on the S 80 casing's ports. With
+one, a model trained on 0016 added a second mirror after the first pair of the suction port.
+
 Neither family produces a composition upstream holds out (goals.heldout_composition): no
 boss_box at all, no mirrored hole_std, no patterned pocket_rect.
 
